From 47ef3f50373b06639832232e4ad0fd19c3a72c52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 23:56:16 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] ui: separate elevated surfaces by step, hairline and rim
 light

Zed's elevated surface gets no background step at all -- elevated_surface and
surface are byte-identical in One -- leaving a black drop shadow as the only
depth cue, which a dark canvas swallows. That is the mechanical cause of the
flat look. Depth is now carried by a background step and a 1px hairline first,
with a shadow only for e2/e3, plus an inset rim on the top edge: on a dark
background the rim light is what actually sells elevation.

The chokepoint is the real fix. elevated() and elevated_borderless() hard-coded
elevated_surface_background and used the ElevationIndex only for the shadow, so
elevation_1/2/3 all painted the same colour and ElevationIndex::bg() was dead
code. Fixing the palette would have changed nothing while the helper never asked
the enum which step it was on. They now call index.bg(cx) and take their radius
from the Zeo token.

Surface and EditorSurface still return no drop shadow -- that is upstream's
deliberate design, and the fix for flatness is the step and the rim, not a shadow
there. The e2/e3 stacks are Zed's own values (peak alpha 12%), kept as-is.

bg() is widened from &mut App to &App: elevated() holds only &App and its
signature is frozen by 71 call sites. bg() only reads theme colours, and every
sibling accessor already takes &App.

Re-skins pickers, the command palette, popovers, modals, context menus and
toasts across 71 call sites in 47 files, with zero call sites modified.

Covers R2.2, R2.4, R2.5, R2.6, R1.2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
